To force a text field to display text in columns using Adobe JavaScript, you can use the `setColumns` method of the `TextField` class. Here's an example of how you can do this:

```javascript
// Assuming you have a text field with the instance name "myTextField"
var myTextField = this.myTextField;

// Set the number of columns you want to display
var numColumns = 2;

// Set the text field to display text in the specified number of columns
myTextField.setColumns(numColumns);
```

In this example, `myTextField` is the instance name of the text field you want to modify. The `setColumns` method takes an integer value that represents the number of columns you want to display. In this case, we set it to 2, so the text will be displayed in two columns. You can adjust the `numColumns` variable to display the text in the desired number of columns.

